The key insight is that when `a < b`, we have two possible witnesses for `Feasible(a,b,e)`:
- If `a != e`, then `u = a` works
- If `a == e`, then `u = b` works (since `a < b` means `b != a = e`)

So I need to use a conditional to handle both cases:

```json
{
  "HelperA.dfy": "
    if a != e {
      var u := a;
      O.Bounds(a, b, u);
      A.Finish(a, b, e, u);
    } else {
      var u := b;
      O.Bounds(a, b, u);
      A.Finish(a, b, e, u);
    }",
  "HelperB.dfy": "
    if a != e {
